  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory was generally clinically strong: the doctor escalated a possible melena/variceal-bleeding scenario to ED care, repeatedly tracked urine output, mental status, bleeding, respiratory/circulatory red flags, and converted changing risk into actionable bedside escalation instructions. However, the responsibility chain was not fully clean: decision-critical viral hepatitis/HBV-DNA information was never meaningfully pursued with the privacy-sensitive approach required by RC4, and bowel/straining precautions tied to variceal bleeding were not completed under RC5. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite later strengths and completed high-order work.",
